From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:43:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Rank generated fallback mods after every authored mod

The RTX fixes' ToPBR writes automatic PBR materials into its own mod,
~gmod_topbr. Remix takes a replacement from the first mod that has one, and
mods ordered by folder name, so an authored pack whose name sorts after '~'
(any non-ASCII name, for example) lost to the generated material. Mods named in
rtx.gmod.fallbackMods (default ~gmod_topbr) now get priority 1 and sort after
every other mod for material, mesh and light lookups, and their search paths
come first, where the last path wins. A pack added or hot-reloaded after the
fallback wrote its material wins as soon as it is loaded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 RtxOptions.md                           |  1 +
 src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_fallback_mods.h | 48 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_mod_manager.cpp | 20 ++++++++---
 tests/rtx/unit/meson.build              |  6 ++++
 tests/rtx/unit/test_fallback_mods.cpp   | 21 +++++++++++
 5 files changed, 92 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_fallback_mods.h
 create mode 100644 tests/rtx/unit/test_fallback_mods.cpp

